= Capital for investment

The credit instrument is a large project: 2 B of building for 2 months, then 1 B to run, and +5 to the credit target while it works. The variants differ in who pays and who must agree: one financing, one cost, one effect.

[+ pl_gc_budget +]

[+ pl_gc_projects +]

- @public
- @banks
- @cooperative
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@public
title: Public fund
subtitle: The state pays everything: 2 B of building, 1 B to run.
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.optionStatus(Q, 'investment_fund', 'public').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_investment_fund_public_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishProjects.chooseOption(Q, 'investment_fund', 'public');
!}
go-to: result

@banks
title: Agreement with banks and industry
subtitle: The state pays half of the building: 1 B, then 1 B; business pressure −8. Needs credit of at least 40.
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.optionStatus(Q, 'investment_fund', 'banks').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_investment_fund_banks_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishProjects.chooseOption(Q, 'investment_fund', 'banks');
!}
go-to: result

@cooperative
title: Cooperative financing
subtitle: Credit for farms and small workshops through cooperatives. The cooperatives of PPS come with stage 5.
choose-if: {! return PolishProjects.optionStatus(Q, 'investment_fund', 'cooperative').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_investment_fund_cooperative_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishProjects.chooseOption(Q, 'investment_fund', 'cooperative');
!}
go-to: result

@result
new-page: true

